   147	They were an hour getting off that turf. Seln went round the knots on three boxes. Brom was got onto his feet between two people and stood there, swaying a little, until the ground had agreed to stay under him. Nobody hurried him. Karis rolled the hide, and then unrolled it a hand's breadth to look once more at a strip of bare skin beyond her last dot, and rolled it again.
