   149	Cael was the last to leave the grey stone. He looked down the ruts to the reeds, and along the pale straight path, to four walls standing in water with the morning in them. A thing lay under those walls with four bolts in it. It would go its round again, he supposed, once in a quarter of an hour, when it was able; and no carter would ever know that anybody had been in.
