+- Bare `as`: every occurrence was heard in context. The possible name-led constructions (`as Pike counted`, `as Karis did`, `as Cael had seen`, `as Lira had taught`, `as Seln had counted`) are manner/comparison clauses, not ambiguous substitutes for “while.”
+- Season/calendar: no season name, month name, month order or English weekday appears. Generic `season` and cold term are compliant. Measures use feet, yards, paces, strides, cords, hands, fathoms and furlongs.
