editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:176:**Vocabulary** (this series' own): fragment, notice, integration, acquisition (directed), engagement (clinical — non-hostile), Path, declaration, tier, rank, Copper/Iron/Bronze/Silver/Gold, Arbiter, sigil, idle state, deployment, the hold, discharge, the reading (surface / deep), mending, reserve, the line, quiet ground → the Quieting, perimeter, radius, stake, the board, HOLD, outcome, the wall. The system's voices are the **log** (Cael's inventory), the **notice** (one only, the tenth), and **Pike's ledger lines**. Interface text appears only where the canon calls for it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:180:**How the first third teaches hard without spending anything:** the log's inventory of nine, with each fragment's idle rent named (Shadow at dusk, Anchor wanting doorways, Storm heavy); the discipline of holding as a skill with failure modes; the board's arithmetic (outcome, not tier); the carters' "don't declare"; the ford's discharge finding; the shale-backs' flight; Oryn's Tide taught in full (contact only, the reserve, three mendings a day, cannot heal herself, "cannot mend what I can't read," two readings); tier talk at the plank (Pike's Copper Force, Teague's unreported Bronze, Lira's Iron R1, Brom's Copper forever). **Cael deploys nothing in M1–M3 except the single ford burst.** The log reads "Deployment since the Line: one" from day 53 to day 90, and the edition keeps that count.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:188:| **Shadow-adjacent** (sealed) | Drifts at dusk in M1–M4 and is held. **Used exactly twice:** M5 ten strides to reach Karis (the informed B6 circle only; Oryn cannot see or attribute the use) [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit B2]; M7 up the stair and across the bowl, unseen by the rim, never attributable | Costs from waking; the seal's whole logic is restated once (M2 log) and honored |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:192:| **Tide-adjacent (NEW, the tenth)** | M5 day 100 the deep reading; **the notice** (verbatim, §10); M6 cost: three days of *listening*, not pulling (his own current at the edge of thought; the nine audible as flows); the idle state learned by the third night; **the first self-reading** (a place near the middle that does not flow; location only; not named); M7 ask refused at the lean-to, granted on the road; the first reading of another person (Oryn: banks, one channel, a current that runs *to* things); M8 the second and third self-readings; **"the still place"** (the phrase appears first here); told to Oryn with his hand on her wrist; **Teague not read** | Contact only; surface at a count of ten, deep only with the subject still, whole and willing; does nothing in a fight; *ask first, every time*; "Things you keep touching don't heal" |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:206:| M1 | The Thornwater stretch at dusk: a mile with a grey shape at forty-five yards, nobody declaring [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2] | 3,500–4,000 | Tension set piece; no blow struck |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:234:**Reader Standard (outranks voice):** clean language, moral clarity, violence with cost and no gore, no innuendo. Carry the source's Gate-27 WATCH notes into the retelling. The ford witness who "got his hand across his own throat somehow" must read unambiguously as *not* self-inflicted (he got his hand between the jaws and his throat). Name the den's remains in one clause. Blood once, as stakes. Cael's decision to read Oryn without consent is named as wrong by him and by three others before it happens.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:240:Callbacks confirmed in Book 8's closed prose: Oryn's letter and "Find me at Thornwater." / "Bring the map." (B8 Ch1, Ch24); "a tape and a season" (B8 Ch1); "Lie still when I say" (B8 Ch18, Ch24); Brom's "Twice… not three times this season" (B8 Ch6); "A measurement is a fact about a ruler, not about the hand that held it." (B8 Ch1, Ch5, Ch20); Hesk's "true to a hair" / "draw a line through it" / "Mind the shape" (B8 Ch1, Ch17, Ch18, Ch22, Ch24); "too small" (B8 Ch16, Ch17, Ch24); "Stop touching it." (B8 Ch7); "Not the Quiet." (B8 Ch7, Ch24); "He'll speak to you when you've cost him something" (B8 Ch7); Teague's after-thaw term [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2] (B8 Ch1, Ch17); "Eleventh" (B8 Ch1, Ch12, Ch17); "the Bronze from Ardenmere" (B8 Ch7); ninety-six in hand (B8 Ch1); fifty-two sheets and forty-one kinds (B8 Ch9–11). Canon documents quote "Three points make a line. Four make an argument.", "Someone made this pattern.", the looms finding, "A circle is a made shape." and the stratum limit. Every other item below is a signature line or document of this book. **Keep them all exact.** Speaker attributions may be re-staged; the words may not.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:243:- Pike's Thornwater-road line (Ch1): *Thornwater road, the stretch. Walked ahead of one cart, one carter, one mule. Delivered at the fence. No losses. Nine marks, paid.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:244:- Pike's ford line (Ch3–4): *Stillhound pack, Thornwater ford: cleared. Five confirmed. Crew of five, four injured, none lost. Price paid.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:245:- Pike's traverse line (Ch8): "High traverse, Oxhollow to Thornwater. Mapped. Delivered at the ford. Carts go round." … "Cart lost. Crew of five, three hurt, none lost. Seventy." … *less six, the cart.* — "Seventy's what the ford paid. Sixty-four's what the job was worth. That's what goes on the wall."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:246:- The Fallow slip (Ch8, Ch12): *Recovery. Surveyor's instruments abandoned at a site on the Fallow road. East of Thornwater; the second day; where the road leaves its line at the rise and comes back to it. One hundred marks (one hundred).* Seal: a hook and a bar, in dark wax.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:248:- The Stair slip (Ch17): *Recovery. Surveyor's instruments abandoned at a site on the Stair road. South of Lowmarch; the first day; where the road drops off the ridge and the ground opens. Three hundred marks (three hundred).*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:269:- **Oryn's letter (Ch24):** *Route's whole. The knee held. Nobody died of three weeks. After the thaw: bring the map, and lie still when I say. — O.* — then: Six, by letter. (The architecture and series docs still quote "eleven days"; prose and Book 8 say **three weeks**. See C6.) [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:278:- Ch8, Part-1 summary (EXC-B7-001): *Twelve weeks. Seven contracts. Pike says there's ground out here where the Arbiter goes quiet, and nobody goes in twice. Karis has been waiting her whole life for a sentence like that. Seln says the contract was written by someone from inside. I say it pays. Two days east, through Thornwater, on the day the healer said. For twelve weeks nothing out here has read me. I'd like to see what a place that reads nothing does with that.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:279:- Ch9, at the stone: *Quiet ground. Karis's Arbiter stopped at a line she can mark with a rock. So did Lira's, Brom's, Seln's, Oryn's — same line, same step. Mine didn't. Mine's been stopped since I was fourteen. I don't know what that means. Nobody asked. Tomorrow we go in.* [OWNER-pending #49]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:280:- Ch10: *The circle is perfect. The stakes are the registry's. The dogs are inside. Everyone's Path dies at the line and mine didn't, and I've told nobody, and I'm going to need to think about why I haven't. Not tonight. Tonight we're inside the one place on the continent where a stillhound can't lose.* [OWNER-pending #49]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:283:- Ch13, the covenant, whole: *Written before. Tomorrow morning, the back room, the door shut. Oryn runs the long reading. Both hands, all of her, all of me, twenty minutes. I lie still. I'm still and whole for the first time in front of her; she said so in the yard, with the tape off.* / *The conditions, as I have them. Sustained: twenty minutes at contact is longer than any bout I've stood. Stakes: I'm three days off the Ring and the nine are still settling; she's three mendings down and her route's late at the far end and she's spending a fourth on a patient who's given her nothing four times. Earnest: she'll do the thing she does as well as she does it. Karis: the model says real, not fight. I don't know if the model's right. Nobody does. Tomorrow's the first time it could be tested and I'm the test.* / *The price. She doesn't know what I am. She can't consent to what she can't know about — not won't; can't. There's nothing I could put in front of her tonight that she could say yes or no to, because the thing doesn't have a name she's heard. I've decided not to tell her before. My reasons are good, and they're the reasons of somebody who wants it, and the real one is that I don't know what she'd say. Entered.* / *If it takes what she's using on me, it takes it from the one person on this road who came to help. I don't know what it costs a source. It's never shown. Tomorrow's the first time it could, and if it does, she pays, and I chose that for her.* / *After: I tell her. In full. On her table, before I'm off it. Whatever it costs me, including the route walking north without me on it.* / *I want it. Write that too.* / *Write it before, not after. That's the whole difference between me and the system.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:284:- Ch14, the birthday line: *Hundred and second day past the Line. Nineteen. Written at Thornwater, in the steading's common room, the fire lit for us. Witnesses: four of my own, and a healer who's a stop.* [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:285:- Ch14, the words retired: *Still open. Still real. Now I can see it. That's worse. The tenth fragment lets me feel my own currents, and there's one in the place session nine logged, and it isn't the tenth, and it isn't any of the nine. It was there before Oryn. It was there before Brom's read caught it. I don't know what it is. I know where it is now. Patience is over; observation begins.* — and *Daeva's rematch, Reydan's answer — both ride east. Nineteen. Ten fragments. Hesk's package is on a ferry somewhere. The last one said mind the shape. I'm starting to.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:289:- Ch18: *Hundred and thirteenth day, the fork above Millrace. Oryn came. On her terms. She'll turn north the day she has to and I won't ask her not to.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:292:- Ch22, the still place: *Read myself. Ten currents, and I can't find the banks either — Oryn's right. And the anomaly's there. Not a fragment. Not a flow. A still place, and the rest of me has been going around it since before I knew it existed. It isn't the Quiet. The Quiet is outside me and turns Paths off. This is inside me and the Paths — the fragments — go around it like they were built to. I don't know what it is. I know it was there before Oryn, before Brom's read, before the ring. Session nine caught the edge of it. I'm not going to guess. Guessing is what the registry did to me. Observation, then the log, then patience.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:294:- Ch23: *Hundred and twenty-second day, the fork. Oryn north. On her terms. I didn't ask. Five on the bearing.* — *I love this country.* — and the crest: *Four sites. One line. The last one's twice the size and the Compact fenced it. The bearing runs through it and keeps going. Karis says four points is an argument. I say it's a bearing — the kind their maps draw as nothing. Home is Lowmarch now. I just wrote that without noticing. Nineteen, ten fragments, a still place at the center of me, and a line on a map that somebody drew before there were maps. We're not done. We're oriented.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:295:- Ch24, the inventory: *Ten confirmed fragments.* / *Wind-adjacent — Lira. Pressure-adjacent — the Bronze from Ardenmere. Iron-adjacent — Brom. Compression-adjacent — Reydan. Ember-adjacent — Karis. Shadow-adjacent — Seln; source protected; the seal held past the Line as it held inside, and was used twice out here where no one who could carry it west could see it, and that is the seal's whole logic and it is unchanged. Storm-adjacent — Daeva. Anchor-adjacent — unnamed; the hand with no face; opened a door on a rim and held a floor in a hall, and I own a piece of the craft the system uses to hold people and have used it twice this year, once each way. Blade-adjacent — Ephram. Tide-adjacent — Oryn; partial; Iron; self and contact; the tenth, and the first that does nothing in a fight, and the only one whose engagement field says clinical, and the only one with a rule on it in her hand and mine: ask first, every time. Deployment notes current on all ten.* / *One anomaly. Session nine. Tide-adjacent. Not an entry any more; a location. The still place. Read three times. Doesn't flow. Doesn't change. Everything goes around it. Not the Quiet. Not a fragment. Older than the log. Observation continues.* / *Reydan will get his answer. Daeva will get her rematch. Both are going to need a map.* — **Audio rule:** Feryn's name never appears in a list run beside Oryn's; every inventory says "the Bronze from Ardenmere."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:298:- Ch1: "You're paper, aren't you" … "Then you know how to keep quiet. Keep it." — Seln: "Don't declare anything." — Lira: "I could clear it." / "No," said Seln. / "I know. I'm saying it so I've said it." — The carter: "First crew I've hired that knew to shut up." — "Stillhound." … "It's a stillhound. You shut up. It went home."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:303:- Ch6: Lira: "That was me," … "The loud thing." — Oryn: "Who's worst?" … "Name's Oryn." … "Tide. Healer." … "Iron. Four, if anybody's keeping a book up here." … "That's one," … "Hands on. That's the only way it works." — "Your ribs are broken," she said. "I can feel that they're broken. I can't feel *you*." … "Whatever you are, I can't read it." … "I've never said that to anyone. Tape them. They'll heal on their own." … "They always have, haven't they?" / "Yes," he said. / "That's not an answer," Oryn said. "That's a *finding*."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:304:- Ch7: Oryn: "That's a tape and a season. It'll set." — "Twenty days," … "Round. Two at a hold, near enough, and the road between, and the road's the part that doesn't move." — "I remember who I've had my hands on," … "That's the book. A healer who needs a page to know who's owed has stopped looking at them." — "In the city I healed Bronzes with bruises. Out here I set legs. I'm not going back and I'm not stopping. The route is the only thing I own." — "It's like putting my hands in a river in the dark. Something's moving. I can't find the banks, so I can't read it, so I can't touch it. That's the rule. I didn't make it." — "When you're not broken, I run the long one. It won't read you either. I want to feel it not read you properly." — "Thornwater's on my route in nine days. You'll be on the board by then. Come find me. I want to read you when you're not broken." / "Nine days." — The ford-keeper: "Then they go round," … "That's worth seventy to know before the first cart's in the gorge. I'd sooner pay it for this." — Teague: "You cleared Thornwater's ford with five and lost a cart on the high bench with five." / "Yes." / "The ford was good work. The bench was a cart." … "The board's going to have you and me on the same contract inside a season. Be good enough that I'm glad."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:305:- Ch8: Pike: "Quiet ground's where the sigil goes to sleep. Yours. Everyone's. You walk a road, and there's a place on it where your Arbiter stops — not slows; stops — and you walk on past and it's back. There's a handful of them. Along the void roads, all of them. Carters walk round them, and have as long as there've been carters. The dogs live in them. Stillhounds. Nobody's asked them why. Why any of it, nobody knows and nobody's needed to, because the rule's *don't go in*, and the rule's never once failed anybody who kept it." … "That's what a carter knows. That's what I know. There's not a man on the ferry knows a word more." — "I've walked past the Fallow Ring two hundred times. Never once stepped over the line. Thirty years on the roads and I've never met a practitioner who did it twice." — Karis: "What's the line?" / Pike: "You'll know," he said. "Your Arbiter tells you. It stops." — Seln: "Somebody wrote this who learned to write inside."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:306:- Ch9: Karis: "Their map has no roads. His has no quiet ground. Between them you get the country." — Oryn: "You're a stop. I've added you." … "Don't make it a long stop." — At the line: Lira, "It's like the air got thick." Brom, "Like a door closing behind me." Karis, "My Arbiter's gone." Seln, "Back up. Ten paces. Tell me when it comes back." Karis, "Same stride. All of us."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:307:- Ch10: Karis: "Sixty-two cords and twenty strides," … "One thousand three hundred and seventy-four yards, and a piece." … "A circle is a made shape." — Lira: "like a clock that stopped and started again without losing the time." — Seln: "You drive them where you've measured to. Not where you've measured from." … "Five years in the weather. A cold term either side." — Brom: "Skin." — Karis: "It costs nothing. There's nothing to spend." — Seln: "I've a knife and fifteen years. It was never most of what I do." — Oryn: "Nothing. Not nothing in him. Nothing in my hands." … "A healer's hands stop working there." — Cael: "It was dark before," … "It's dark now." — Karis: "None I own. And I own more than the registry prints." — Seln: "They live in here because nothing that walks in can fight." [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:308:- Ch11: Seln: "The road's cut." … "The grass. Where the cord went." — Oryn: "Move," … "I can't fix this here. Move." … "She keeps it." — **The order:** "A mend that deep holds nothing for a season. Nothing. That arm is not to hold. It's not to strike. It's not to catch. Not a rope, not a knife, not a fall, not a friend. Not until I say. And I'll say at first snow, near enough, if it's let alone." … "One arm. From here to the snow." — "The ankle's a tape and a season. I've told you that before." — Close: "It worked in there." / "Yours." / "Yes," Cael said. / "Later." / "Later."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:309:- Ch12: Seln: "They surveyed it," … "Five years ago by the stake, maybe six. They paced the circles and stamped the stakes and drew the maps with holes where the circles are. That's not ignorance. Ignorance doesn't stamp iron." — "The Compact knows what quiet ground does," … "And it's filed somewhere we can't reach." — "No," … "I carried the maps. I never saw the file. I'm not going to draw you one." — Karis (written): *Blank. Stamped. Filed.* — Seln: "We just told them. The report goes west on the next ferry. It'll say we came out." — Oryn: "Six is wrong. I'm a stop." / "They'll write six," Seln said. — Oryn: "I can't mend what I can't read. That's the rule."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:310:- Ch13: Oryn: "You don't get a yes. You get told." — Karis: "Ephram fought you in earnest and the notice said non-hostile. This is earnest and it isn't a fight at all." … "The model doesn't say the engagement has to be a fight. It says it has to be real." — Seln: "That's not consent. It's the nearest thing to it the log's ever had, and it's still not it. I'd enter both." — Lira: "She asked to read you," … "She didn't ask for the rest. Those aren't the same sentence." — Oryn's twenty-minute report: "I can feel that there's movement. More than one. I can't count them — I can't find where one stops. There's no channel. Everyone has a channel; I feel the banks and I know the Path. I can't find the banks in you. I've looked for twenty minutes. It isn't that you're broken. It's that I can't find anything shaped like the thing I read." — "Eleven years. I've never had my hands in something and not known what it was." — "Something just changed," she said. "In you. While I was in there." / "Yes." / "Did I do that?" / "No. I did." … "I need to tell you what I am." / "Then lie still while you do it. You've been still for twenty minutes. I want to see if you can manage twenty-one."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:311:- Ch14: "So I couldn't read you because there was nothing in you shaped like a Path for the reading to find." / "I don't know. Maybe." / "I don't know either. I'm a healer, not a theorist." … "What I know is you've now got a piece of the thing I read with." / "Yes." … "Then use it on yourself first. Before anyone." … "I want to know what you find, and I want to be the one you tell." — Oryn: "And when it turns outward, you ask. Every time. I ask the dying." / "I ask first. Every time." — Karis: "You have an instrument now. It's not mine. It never will be. I'm entering that I know that." — Oryn: "A stop," … "Good. Write it down before it changes." — Seln: "Six went in. Six came out. He's counted her." … "So has the broker."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:312:- Ch15: *the Quieting* — "A personal spiritual entity should not fail the way five looms fail when somebody shuts the sluice on the wheel that drives them." — *identically* — Seln: "Six sigils on the road that day," … "Five went out." … "I'm not filing that either. I'm counting it." — Karis's struck six: *one dark since fourteen; no change either side of the line; stated by him, not tested by me* — **The stratum limit, the book's only [UNBOUND]:** "It's older, I'll say once and not again, than [UNBOUND] — older than the word they retired, and I can't say by how much. Entered as a limit, not a finding. We explained the middle of the story in Ostrand. This is before the beginning, and I don't have a ruler for it." — Brom: "Say it with less." / Karis: "Everything I can date, I've dated. The floor's under all of it. I don't know how far." — "I have a hypothesis and I'm not entering it, because entering it would make it a finding, and it isn't one. It's a fear." … Lira: "Does it help? Not writing it." / "No," Karis said. "It's just correct." — "The circle's perfect," … "Perfect isn't natural. Somebody made a floor that turns Paths off. It's older than anything I can date. And it doesn't turn you off. Three facts. I'm not putting a verb between them." … "I'm not," Karis said. "I'm saying it to you. That's different." [OWNER-pending #49]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:313:- Ch16: Lira: "You told me when you knew. You don't know. So you told me *that*. Keep doing it." … "It scares you." / "Out there I was the thing the system couldn't hold." … "In there I was the only thing that *worked*. I don't know which one's worse." / "The second one. You're allowed to say so." — Seln: "They know something turns Paths off. They *don't* know something doesn't turn off. Yet." — Oryn: "My hands stop at that line. Yours don't. I had my hands in you for twenty minutes and I can tell you what I didn't find, which is a Path. That's all I've got." … "I'm not going to guess past it." — Karis: "We find the others. All of them. And we find out whether they're the same." … "That's how you find a handful. One at a time, for money." — Oryn: "Don't go in without me. Not because I'm any use inside. Because somebody should be outside the line who can put an arm back on." — Brom: "That's not comfort," … "I don't do that. It's a count. You like counts." — Oryn: "Once is a morning." … "Don't read anyone on the road to find out whether you can."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:314:- Ch17: Pike: "Eleventh. Teague's ten up." … "I'd not take it." — Seln: "That's not a wage. That's a lure, cut to fit." … "This isn't a contract. It's a pre-restriction inventory. They've mapped what we do inside, and they've priced a floor where we can't do it." / Karis: "They don't know about Cael." / "They don't need to." … "They want the case. The boy's the price of the case." — "They'll send people. A lure's no use if nobody's waiting at the end of it. People have faces. Six years I've wanted a face." — Cael: "Inside the circle, I'm the only one who works. They chose a floor that makes the rest of you helpless. They don't know it doesn't do anything to me." — Brom: "Doors open both ways," … "I don't like it. I'm in." — Lira: "I want it entered that I said walk away. I was right. We're going anyway." — Teague: "You're taking the Stair contract." / "Yes," Cael said. / "It's a bad contract." / "Yes." … "My crew's at Millrace in two days," Teague said. "If you're late back, we'll come look." / "Noted." [OWNER-pending #50]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:315:- Ch18: Oryn: "No." … "You asked. That's the rule and you kept it. The answer's no. Next." — "You're asking me to break the route," / "I'm not asking. I'm telling you where we'll be." / "That's worse. That's a healer's sentence." — "I'm not going to be anybody's sixth." — **Terms:** "You're on the route now. Which means when I say lie still, you lie still, and when I say I can't help you, you believe me." — "Well?" / "May I read you?" / "Yes. That's the answer, and I'm the one giving it…" — "You're built to arrive." / "Yes," she said. "That's what I am." — Lira: "He asked twice and got one," / Brom: "That's the rate," — Seln: "Newer. This one's been re-surveyed."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:316:- Ch19: Brom: "Ridge," — Seln: "They can shoot the bowl," … "They can't shoot the stair." — Oryn: "I can see what's wrong. I can't feel it and I can't touch it. Tape it. Leave the bolt." … "the bolt's the plug" … "I came south for exactly this. Enter that." — Oryn: "Ask first," — Lira: "Later." / "Later." — Oryn at the stone: "There. Back," … "The clock started again." — "It held a stair. It's not going to hold anything else this season." — Seln: "No faces." — Teague: "You walked out of the Quiet declaring," / "Yes." … "Then you're not on the board anymore. You're something the board doesn't have a column for."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:317:- Ch20: Teague: "We'll hold it till you're up." / "Noted" — Oryn: "What are they" / Karis: "Lines," — Karis: "He tried to drive it. Twice, by the head. It wouldn't go. Nothing goes into this." — Seln: "Nobody leaves a registry kit. It's signed out. You don't get another." … "I don't know what this is in, and I'm not going to say." — Karis: "Forty-one," … "every ten cords and a piece. Two hundred and twenty yards and a stride, to the stride." … "The floor was carved by somebody who knew the circle's size," … "A measurement is a fact about a ruler, not about the hand that held it." [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:318:- Ch21: Oryn: "Big. Under. Comes up. Nobody's seen it whole." — Seln: "It's blind. It reads weight on the floor. It strikes where the weight is. And it strikes what *stays*." — Karis: "It reads that as the heaviest thing on the floor," / Cael: "It reads that as the thing that *stays*," — Lira: "We're going in without Paths to look at walls with a thing under the floor." / "Yes," Karis said. / "Just checking that's the plan." — Seln: "It's blind. It reads the floor. Get *off* the floor." — "You're copying," / "I'm not getting another chance," / "No, I can see that you're not," — *A thing that hunts what stays commits to the thing that stays hardest.* — "Brom," Cael said. "Wall. Your weight. Now." — Oryn: "Twice. It'll hold twice. It will not hold three times this season, so don't ask it to" — "You went in the water." / "You went in for Brom." / "Brom's on my route." … "So are you." … "Lie still. I want to read you."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:319:- Ch22: Oryn: "A still place that everything goes around. I've never felt that in anyone." / "Is it wrong?" / "I don't know what right would look like in you. Nobody does. That's not a comfort; it's a finding." … "Write it down and stop touching it. Things you keep touching don't heal." — Teague's healer: "Twice?" … "Then it wants binding, not hands," — Teague: "What are you." / Cael: "Why did you stop reporting?" / "Because the board pays the same whether I do or don't," … "and the registry doesn't, and I'd sooner be worth what I did than what they wrote." … "That's not an answer to mine." / "No." / "You didn't answer." / "I don't have one. Neither does the board. You said so." / "I did." … "The board's going to need a new column."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:320:- Ch23: Karis: "Three points make a line. Four make an argument." — "That's a healer's sentence," Oryn said … "I know whose it is," — Brom, Lira, Oryn at the first halt: "Twice," / "Twice," / "And not three," — Oryn at the fork: "I'm three weeks late there…" … "I've been a stop on my own route for nine days. I'm going back to being the route." … "Find me at Thornwater," … "Bring the map," — Karis: "Half the bend is twice the round. Four hundred. Near enough. Twice the radius. The same shape, at twice the size, round a thing I can't see." — Seln: "That's not a survey. That's a cordon. They've been here more than once." — Lira: "Twice the size. Is it twice the *anything else*?" — Cael: "Not without her. Not without knowing what a circle twice the size does to the four of you. And not without the map finished." / "It's finished," Karis said. "It's a line." / "Then it's a line that points somewhere. We go home and find out where."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:321:- Ch24: Pike: "Teague says you need a column I don't have. I've kept this ledger thirty years. First time it's been wrong about a crew by being too small." — the carters: "Eleventh," / "Aye," — Teague: "After the thaw. Whatever's on that bearing. My crew comes." / "Noted," — Pike: "Fence. Forty. Teague says it's yours if you want it; he's got the cold road," / Brom: "Ours," — Lira: "She'll say when," / Brom: "After the thaw," — *The sites were on an alignment. Not random.* — Karis: "Someone made this pattern." (said once; nobody answers) — **Closing, exact:** "I have ten things that aren't a Path," Cael said, eventually, to nobody in particular, "no tier, no rank, no file I can see — and five people, one of them on a route, who've walked into the quiet three times and come out." He turned it over once and let it stand. "And a line on a map that somebody drew before there was a registry to draw one." / Lira, one-armed, feeding the fire: "Then we follow it." / Brom: "After the thaw." / Karis, writing: "Noted." / Down the fire, the man who used to file reports about him watched the snow on the ferry landing with evident professional approval and said nothing, which — from him — was home. / Nothing out here had read him. At three floors older than any registry, every Path in the party had stopped at a line and his had not; a fourth had been paced from outside and not crossed. Nobody alive — least of all him — knew why. Someone had made the pattern. That was as far as anyone could say. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48] [OWNER-pending #49]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:334:| The Quieting's source (Architect reset; B10–11) | Observable mechanics only: perfect circle, about 220 yards [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2], sharp line, identical failure, fused floors, carvings, fauna denning | Spread; growth; any city; any change in a site's size |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:342:| Teague's crew | Roles, small beats, the young one at the shafts | Any name (Book 8 says the young one's name once and does not enter it) |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:350:- **C1 · The cart, the horse and the purse vanish across the seam.** The edition's Book 6 ends (ch60) with a cart, a brown gelding, three boxes and a case under one canvas, and a pooled purse larger than Cael had expected. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: coordinator ruling] B7 never mentions the cart or horse. The boxes ride a carter's grain (Ch1); the crew hires the smith's cart (Ch5); by day 49 they have "Eighteen marks earned and about ten left after the jug" and sleep in the meadow. **OWNER #23 (binding):** stage it in M1. The horse is a city animal on mule roads (fodder, noise, "paper" written on it), and the cart is too wide for the scrub ruts past Lowmarch. They are sold in Lowmarch's first week. The sale and what remains of the Book 6 purse become a sealed **reserve** that the crew agrees not to live on (Brom's rule: we eat what the board pays). The log's "in hand" counts only the board purse, so every figure in the prose and in Book 8 stands. This is no longer pending. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit N7]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:351:- **C2 · The crew's mule.** From Ch16–17 the crew has "a mule" while Oryn has gone north "with … the mule's spare rope in her hand for the next hold's beast." At Millrace there are two mules; at the fork Oryn takes one and the crew keeps one, which stays in the ferryman's shed through the cold term (Book 8). [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2; unlisted named-season hit found by the item-16 grep, same substitution as line 40] **Recommend:** stage Oryn's decision at Thornwater (day 110–111). She leaves her own mule with the crew for the boxes and a one-armed girl, and takes the route's beast at Millrace. An Oryn decision beat; no prose fact changes.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:355:- **C6 · Oryn's lateness and the letter.** Ch12's "The route's eleven days north of here" and Ch15's "nine days late here and eleven at the next" do not reconcile (seams F5a, accepted as spoken). Ch18 projects Thornwater "eleven days late"; the closed prose then says **three weeks** at the fork (Ch23) and in the letter (Ch24), and Book 8 Ch1 quotes "Nobody died of three weeks." The architecture card and `series/THE_FRACTURED_PATH_SERIES.md` still say "eleven days." **The edition protects "three weeks."** Recommend writing Ch12's figure as a distance ("the far end of the route is eleven days north of here") and keeping the lateness arithmetic honest from day 104 (nine and eleven) to day 110 (Oxhollow seventeen) to the fork (three weeks).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:357:- **C8 · The Tide stall.** The bible (PROVISIONAL) defines a combat stall that Oryn "has done three times in her life." Neither Book 7 nor Book 8 shows it. **Recommend:** at most one mention, in Oryn's teaching in M3 as a limit she names and hates. Never used, since she is never made to fight. Owner may prefer omission.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:361:- **Already resolved in the prose (do not reopen):** the Lowmarch–Thornwater road is two days; the rib clock (tape off on the 99th at "twenty-one days"); cash 116 → 108 → 102 → 96; Ch23 at the fork is four people and one mule; the sling is "five weeks"; Millrace (EXC-B7-003); the arrested stake (EXC-B7-004); the outer-coping trials (EXC-B7-005); "Twelve weeks" (EXC-B7-001); "two weeks old" (EXC-B7-002); Lira holds Oryn's crossbow from the Hall, not the fork.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:368:**All canon names are kept**, including Bracken in Ephram's letter. **No new proper names are proposed.** The expansion is designed so that every new person is a role. **Do not name:** any member of Teague's crew (the spear, the bow with the limp, the young one, the older healer of no Path); the steading's woman and the bowman at Thornwater; the carters (the Thornwater carter, the carter's wife, the hide carter); the westbound courier at the ford; the ferryman and his boy; the smith and his boy; the landing broker and his clerk; the hide-woman; the crew of three and the mule-named crew on the wall; the ford-keepers at Oxhollow and Millrace; the miller; the old woman with the knee; the child three stops on; the four unnamed holds on Oryn's route; the six on the rim and the second Anchor specialist; the eleven-bale captain and the north-road woman captain. Site names stay descriptive (the Fallow Ring, the Long Stair, the Drowned Hall, **the fourth site**, unnamed). Fauna stay compound nouns (stillhound, shale-back, wold-wyrm).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:372:**By-ear watch list for the audiobook (carried from the registry):** Feryn and Oryn never in one list run ("the Bronze from Ardenmere"); the Oryn / Oxhollow / Ostrand O-stack; Pike / Fiske; Stair / (Book 8's) Span. Avoid putting Oxhollow and Oryn in one short sentence where it can be helped.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:8:- Owner names: canon only. The steading's woman, the bowman, the Thornwater carter, the carter's wife (and the boy on her board), the woman captain, the crew of three: all unnamed.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:16:The second morning after the wall (day 51). Teague's crew went out at the previous dawn on the autumn road and is a week away. The five are thirteenth of thirteen with about ten marks, sleeping in the meadow. Nobody is hurt. Karis holds one word, *stillhound*, underlined.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:27:- **Thornwater, days 54–58:** the calf in elevens; the ladder inventory each morning; Brom carrying nothing for the first time Cael can remember; Karis's barn-table library (three boxes made into shelves with no wall) — "everything I know about the wrong country"; **the cart-yard** (the man with the clouded eye who does not talk roads to paper; the carter's wife: "Everybody knows the quiet ground. Nobody goes in."; *everybody knows* underlined twice; "Not a good one. The first."). The grain moves.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:29:- **Lowmarch, day 60:** fourteen slips. Seln reads the board and takes the well: "I keep waiting for someone to ask for my report." **Brom at the plank's end:** "What does the board pay a man with no Path at all." / "Same as anyone… What'd he do?" He writes it on an old slip and keeps it against his skin, the second time in his life (Rooke was the first). Pike: "Held a dog with a shoulder and a river, that one." **The mail** sorted aloud. Hesk's letter (protected), and the grandmother he did not know about. The log. **The saying** at the book, the sheet rewritten by hand: twelfth. "Teague's still eleven up. He'll speak to you when you've cost him something."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:9:- POV: Cael ≈27,300. **Oryn cutaway ≈2,000** (day 100, the stool after the telling, the covenant page on her knee; what a healer does with having been a source; no theory). **Karis cutaway ≈2,600** (the week of tables: the tally of kinds she will not say; *the Quieting* chosen because it is the right grammar; **the pen held over the page, and the hypothesis never stated**). **Lira cutaway ≈2,000** (the bowman's lessons: shooting braced, one-armed, with a bow someone else spans). **Vastin ≈300** (the courtesy copy; three sentences, substance exact). **Oryn cutaway ≈1,800** (dawn on the 111th onward: north out of the gate with a spare rope, having left her mule with the crew; the route, the debt she set, the line she tested; ends before Millrace's table).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:16:Minute twenty-one on a plank table in Thornwater's back room. Ten fragments. A healer who has just felt something change in a patient she cannot read, and who has been told she is about to hear what he is.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:20:The deliberate quieter movement. Its reason: integration cost, the midpoint disclosure and the birthday, between the Ring and the Stair. Its action is learning. Cael turns nineteen with the lights on inside himself; the Quieting gets its name; Lira hears it first; and the instrument gets a rule before it is ever turned outward. Turns and promises:
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:25:- **The birthday (day 102):** Lira instigates one-armed, pays one-handed, and has been practising the pouch for a week without saying so. Brom acquires three kinds ("Three."). Six places in the common room. Oryn at the table "like a woman who has sat at a great many tables and stayed at none of them." **The line written** (protected). "A stop. Good. Write it down before it changes." **Pike's Fallow copy** by carter; "Six went in. Six came out." beside Gault's last note. Hesk's package does not come, and the absence sits at the table unremarked. Seln: "He's counted her… So has the broker." The apples argument, which Karis loses on the merits.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:27:- **The week of tables (days 103–109).** The ring laid flat (eleven sheets cut to the uprights' heights); the tally of *kinds* she will not number from one site. **Five findings, each a scene:** (1) *the Quieting*: grammar for a process, not a place; (2) **identical failure** across five sigils (Iron R1, Copper, no ranking, Bronze, Iron R4; Lira's clock in Lira's words), and the looms sentence, unfiled (protected); Seln's "Six… I'm counting it." and the struck six; (3) **the strata as a physical demonstration** (four chips oldest to the right; the knife marked and the floor didn't; no stroke, no join, no laid edge; weathering past the founding stone), with **[UNBOUND] once** (protected), then Brom's "Say it with less."; (4) **the stakes, once, in four sentences**; (5) **the observation entered and the interpretation stopped**: "It's a fear." / "Does it help?" / "It's just correct." Oryn works the hold in the yard (nine late here, eleven at the next) and looks at the table once.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:28:- **New, a learning arc: Lira and the bowman.** The bowman off the gate-walk (unnamed) teaches her to shoot braced one-armed, against a rail and a knee, with the steading's bow spanned for her because she cannot span one-armed and says so. Short sessions, his few words, her fierce economy. This plants the Hall (M8). Oryn's order is kept exactly: the left arm holds nothing.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:29:- **C2, staged:** Oryn decides to leave her mule with the crew. Three boxes and a girl with one arm need it more than a healer whose holds keep beasts. She will take the next hold's beast at Millrace. Her decision, said in her register.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:30:- **Day 110.** Lira first at the gate-walk at dusk, in the order he has had for fifteen days (protected exchange); the fighter's question ("It felt like a Third-day."); her hand along the plank to his boot; "Then six." **The circle of six**: what each of the four saw, in order; Karis's five findings said; Seln's "Yet."; Oryn's "I'm not going to guess past it."; nobody puts a verb between the facts; the four wheres; "We find the others…"; "One at a time, for money." Oryn: "North in the morning… Don't go in without me…"; her hand on Seln's shoulder. **Brom at the ladder** ("It's a count. You like counts."). **The Vastin window** (three sentences). **Oryn at the well**: the rule written while she watches (protected); "Once is a morning" (the debt's terms set by her: three readings on different days, then all of it at once); "Don't read anyone on the road to find out whether you can."; the note written under the rule. **The second pole** in the log (protected).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:31:- **Oryn's window north (111–112):** the spare rope, the road bending, what she carries in her head. It ends before Millrace.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:45:The sensation-language of listening, kept to sensation; Thornwater in the back of autumn (ice on the trough, the grain going up the ladder past where they sleep); the tables' daily rhythm; the bowman's manner and words; the birthday's warmth and humor; the shape of each finding scene; all the windows.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:49:Dawn on the 111th: Oryn north on a route seventeen days late at Oxhollow, carrying a spare rope; the crew with her mule, three boxes and a hundred and two in hand. A rule on the page and a debt with a date. Ten fragments and one place that doesn't move. "Pike said nobody goes in twice. Tomorrow makes three." The completion report has been on a desk somewhere for eight days.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:8:- Owner names: canon only. The miller, Millrace's ford-keeper and patients, the six on the rim, the second Anchor specialist, the hide-woman, the crew of three and Teague's crew stay unnamed. **No faces on the rim.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:9:- POV: Cael ≈35,400. **Seln cutaway ≈2,200** (night of day 112, after the council: the two slips laid side by side in his head; six years carrying a case for people he cannot see; why he wants a face; he may not open the case or decode anything). **Teague cutaway ≈2,400** (days 113–115: at Millrace, the five not back; the walk south to look; the rim's ground read in lantern light, the crossbows, "declaring"; holding the rim at dawn without being asked; no crew names).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:12:**Read before drafting:** B7 source `chapter-17.md`, `chapter-18.md`, `chapter-19.md`, `chapter-20.md`; `BOOK_MAP.md` §7 (Shadow twice; Anchor unbinding), §8 (Stair allowance), §10 (Ch17–20), §11 (faceless; the rim sees only the outside), §12 C3; `STATE_LEDGER.md` (Movement 6 append); `v3-runs/book-07/CONFLICT-B7-CH18.md` (why Millrace).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:16:First light on the 111th at Thornwater: Oryn gone north, her mule with the crew. Lira is two weeks into the season's order. A completion report sits on a desk west of the Line.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:22:- **Thornwater → Lowmarch (111–112), the first cold.** The fourth honest catalogue from the rise.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:23:- **Pike says the Fallow line before the door is shut;** it costs a line (eleventh; "Teague's ten up"). Then what the wall cannot say: thirty years, forty-odd crews, nobody over a line and back, "Six in and six out, and the sixth a healer." **The room updates** without a word (the hide-woman, the crew of three gone grey, the carter from the first week, the boy). **Teague stands** when they come in and sits at "eleventh."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:26:- **Millrace (day 113):** the wheel heard before the roofs; the ford-keeper's "Five off the ridge" / "I know." **Oryn's table**: fifteen, three serious (a crushed hand, a child's chest, an old woman's knee with a ladder in it) and a dozen small with one hand each. **Ask first, refused** ("You asked. That's the rule and you kept it. The answer's no. Next."), entered first. Karis: "She was curious about you. Enter that somewhere." **Her arithmetic aloud**, finger by finger. "You're asking me to break the route." / "I'm not asking. I'm telling you where we'll be." / "That's worse. That's a healer's sentence." "I'm not going to be anybody's sixth." **Word sent up the route** by carter (late, how late, why, where to send for the child). **Terms** (protected). Lira's sixth-chair line. The fork log.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:29:- **Day 114, the trap (≈9,000–10,500 across two chapters).** The crossing in Seln's order. **The bolt at forty meters**: "Ridge." Six hooded on the rim in road grey (two south, two east, one west, one north). **The Anchor course** closing the line behind them; Cael sees it with perception only. Bolts skip off the fused plate. **Lira runs *down***, and the unit follows. **Forty steps.** The chamber, ten strides square, its ceiling the floor; walls carved; at the middle "something cased… a cord," unread. **The doorway**: "They can shoot the bowl… They can't shoot the stair." **Oryn without hands**: lamp, eyes, two fingers; "Tape it. Leave the bolt."; "the bolt's the plug"; "I came south for exactly this. Enter that." Lira's mend reopened on the stair wall. **The stalemate, given room**: the square of grey going white and grey; a bolt sent down to stop at the thirty-first step; Brom grey and not worse; Karis with her back to the wall she would give a year to read. The design read aloud ("It thinks the floor did the same thing to all six of us."). **The order:** up alone with the one he was given. Oryn: "Ask first." / "I'm not reading anyone." / "I know. I'm saying the rule out loud so it's been said on this floor too." Lira: "Later." **The ascent, Shadow alone**, across the bowl unseen; the rim scanning for a shout that cannot exist. Anchor let off at ten meters as perception, then as a hand: **the knot found and released**, the course going slack like rigging. **Over the stone, declaring**: Wind, Storm seeding the rut, Compression at contact, Ember held out. He removes one man from the plan and does not fight him. The rim breaks as professionals break. The west one looks back for a second, hood up, nothing in it. Four crossbows left; no faces. "Back."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:31:- **Day 115:** Teague holds the rim unasked ("We'll hold it till you're up." / "Noted"). **C3: Karis paces the Stair's perimeter in the morning** with Lira one-armed on the line, under four rim-holders who are theirs, and gets two hundred. **Down with two lamps**: the air at the twentieth step; the chamber catalogued properly; Oryn's "What are they" / "Lines." **The kit**: open, contents in taking-out order, the cord laid toward the east wall, stake thirty-two with the stroke-and-bar beside its mallet, point bright, the floor unmarked (EXC-B7-004: "Twice, by the head… Nothing goes into this."). **The ledger read by Seln**: distances, the radius in their own hand, a designation in an index he does not know, and the last line, *third site confirmed on bearing* —. **Karis's body at "bearing."** Six hours; twenty-nine sheets; "Sheet"; Lira ahead of her every time; **forty-one** (protected); the line *between* the courses at the radius; "A measurement is a fact about a ruler…" **The kit carried up**: Brom refuses help three times. The rim-holders: the spear grounded once. The log at the stone (protected). The straightedge out on the carter's map, not yet touching anything.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:44:The Lowmarch room; Millrace's texture; Oryn's patients; the road lesson's sensation; the chamber's cold; the stalemate's small human business; the ascent's suspense inside the planted rules; the rim action's choreography; the six hours; both windows.
