editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-AUDIT.md:69:### B2. The first planned Shadow use is visible to Oryn before she joins the trusted knowledge circle
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-AUDIT.md:71:- **B7 says:** Shadow is first used at the Ring, “circle and Oryn only” (`BOOK_MAP.md:188`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:74`; `packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:22`, `:31`). Oryn does not learn the mechanism until M6 (`MOVEMENT-005.md:35`; `MOVEMENT-006.md:22`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-AUDIT.md:73:- **Why it matters:** “circle and Oryn only” does not satisfy the term. Oryn is still an outsider when the use occurs, and the current plan gives her line of sight to exactly the tradecraft the seal protects.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-AUDIT.md:75:- **Amend:** restage the Ring use so Oryn cannot see or attribute it: blocked sightline, attention fixed on Lira/Karis, and no observable discontinuity she can carry west. State in the packet that “circle” here means only the already-informed B6 circle. The M6 telling does not automatically waive Seln's term; if the use moves later, the plan must still establish that every observer either cannot see/attribute it or cannot carry the seeing west.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-AUDIT.md:231:4. **Repair capability logic before issuing later packets:** enforce the Anchor range, carry the Gold read's medium choice, and restage Shadow's M5 use so Oryn cannot see or attribute it (B1–B3).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:8:- Owner names: canon only. Oxhollow's ford-keeper, the smith, the patients at Oxhollow's table and Teague's crew stay unnamed. Of Oryn's seven holds, only Oxhollow and Thornwater are named.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:9:- POV: Cael ≈34,200. **Lira cutaway ≈1,800** (day 78, the ledge: the burst her body chose before she did; "That was me. The loud thing."). **Oryn cutaway ≈2,600** (days 84–92: out of Oxhollow's gate north on her route, the carter's hand she owed, the child three stops on, the patient she wants to read whole; she decides to put a day on the route; it ends before Thornwater). **Teague cutaway ≈1,400** (day 84, Oxhollow's ford at dusk: four sentences priced before he says them).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:22:- **The Oxhollow slip** (seventy, on the map, paid at Oxhollow) sorts itself to the top, and he counts why: it pays; nobody's finger is on it; it is *ground*. Pike: take a cart ("You want to tell a ford it holds a cart, you'd better have had one on it."). Seln asks about shale-backs quietly at the plank's end, and Cael does not go to listen. The smith's cart is six against its return. The boxes go because there is nowhere to leave them.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:28:- **Day 80, Oryn**, introduced through her walk and then her hands: "Who's worst?"; the set ("That's the part you'll mind"); the mend in less than an hour (Lira: "Cold… No. It's going along."); she sits as a carter sets down a known load; "That's one."; "Hands on. That's the only way it works… And I can't do it to me."; Brom's wrist ("Then it should have closed in a month and hasn't, because you've pulled on it."); Karis: "Ember. And nothing. You're empty."; "Hm." at the lattice line. **The first failed surface reading** on Cael: she stops in the middle, looks at her hands, tries again, and her face does the instrument's thing. The protected exchange ends on "That's a *finding*."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:30:- **Oxhollow (day 84):** the table under the lean-to, hers twenty days at a time; worst first; "That's three." The map paid seventy ("Then they go round."). **The second and third readings** (ribs knitting with "nothing doing it"; the wrist and neck, nothing wrong, still nothing): "a river in the dark." **The two readings taught before they are load-bearing** (surface: a count of ten; deep: both hands, minutes, still and whole, at a mending's cost; "I don't run it on a road"). If the stall is named (C8 default: at most once), it is a limit she prices and hates, never used. **Three questions** (right places — yes; faster; no healer ever got anything — no). "That's the visit." He has a sentence asking her south and does not say it. "Thornwater's on my route in nine days… I want to read you when you're not broken." / "Nine days."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:31:- **Teague at Oxhollow's ford at dusk:** four lines (protected), not unkind; Cael has no argument. The log. The image: Teague's four walking the ford quiet, and a mule a mile up the north road with a woman on its down-slope side.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:36:- Oryn knows nothing of fragments; no deep reading is run. She records nothing and remembers. Her Tide in full: contact only; about three serious mendings a day, fed and slept (two on a road); cannot heal herself; "cannot mend what I can't read."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:39:- Nobody mentions quiet ground. Oryn's other five holds are not named, here or in her window.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:44:The bench's days and weather; the herd's look and sound; the exact choreography inside the planted geometry (fin, split, cart, boxes); Oryn's first look at each of them; the walk down; the yard at Oxhollow; which patients come to the table; Lira's and Oryn's windows; humor (Brom's "Carrying." / "Not pulling."; Lira on a mule not mentioning the mule).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:48:Day 84: a hundred and sixteen in hand, six owed to the smith for a cart in a gorge. Three ribs taped, a calf bound in her cloth, a leg that is new, an ankle taped, a wrist mended and not to pull. Three failed readings, and a healer who wants a fourth "when you're not broken." Thornwater in nine days. Two people out here are measuring him, and neither has a seal.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:8:- Owner names: canon only. The hide-woman, the landing broker's clerk, the smith, the Thornwater people and Teague's crew stay unnamed.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:12:**Read before drafting:** B7 source `chapter-08.md`, `chapter-09.md`, `chapter-10.md`; `BOOK_MAP.md` §7 (Cael's two private tests), §10, §11 (the "made" sentences, Compact limits); `universe/UNIVERSE_BIBLE.md` (the Quieting, observable mechanics); `STATE_LEDGER.md` (Movement 3 append).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:16:Oxhollow's bank at dusk on the 84th: a hundred and sixteen in hand, and six owed. Ribs taped, the calf bound, Lira's leg new and her right boot gone. Oryn is walking north; Teague's crew has crossed south. Nine days to Thornwater.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:22:- **Six days Oxhollow → Lowmarch (days 84–90), lightly on the page:** the ford walked quiet a day behind Teague's crew; Lira's carter's boot for two marks, packed with linen; the tape hated by noon; Brom keeps the healer's week to the hour and picks up the middle box with both hands on the eighth morning. A small physical problem on the road is optional and the author's.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:23:- **Lowmarch, day 90:** two hold slips with HOLD and **five names** ("Holds came to the ferry. Asked who. I said you."), waiting a fortnight or Teague. The traverse line read and priced: "Sixty-four's what the job was worth." / "Fair." **The posting under the stone's far edge**, the dust-curve on it, the hook-and-bar seal in wax; he reads it upside down, then gives it to Pike. Pike's face stops; Cael counts nine. "That's the Fallow Ring." / "That's quiet ground." **Pike's speech** (protected) and "You'll know. Your Arbiter tells you. It stops." Karis brings the page with two lines under it from the middle box: "A location. And a contract." The smith paid: a hundred and eight. Lira at the roof's edge: "Two hundred times. He counted." / "So do you. I've never once heard you say never."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:24:- **The board's room:** the wall rewritten, tenth; "Teague's nine up… He read that slip yesterday. Read it twice… I'd have done the same, and I told him, and he said he knew." **The council, once, in order:** Karis's case; Brom ("A survey kit's a cart's worth… That's not the reason. That's what it is."); Lira ("I'm saying it's a walk and a carry. I'm not saying it isn't the other thing."); Cael: "It pays."; **Seln reads the paper, not the words**: "Somebody wrote this who learned to write inside." / "It goes in." / "That's not a reason not to go." **The ninety-third**: nobody says *bring her*, and Karis writes "Thornwater, ninety-third. The healer." The Part-1 summary log (protected, "Twelve weeks").
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:26:- **Thornwater, day 93:** Oryn on the bench at the gate with a carter's hand; "Fifteen days. Since the break." / "Breath stops at it." / "Ninth day. I said nine. You've counted." Her **two reasons** (a patient whole and still for the long reading; the carters' claim about a healer's hands, never checked); "You're a stop. I've added you… Don't make it a long stop." Her table that evening, seen from the loft door.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:27:- **Days 94–95, six on the Fallow road** (Oryn on the mule's down-slope side; the registry sheet goes back into the box at the east gate; past Thornwater's fork the printed sheet is white). **The rise:** he looks at the dark place where an Arbiter would be. Lira's hand up: "It's like the air got thick." Brom: "Like a door closing behind me." Oryn's hands half-raised and silent. Karis: "My Arbiter's gone." Seln: "Back up. Ten paces. Tell me when it comes back." Five *backs* at one stride. The stone. **Cael felt nothing, either way, and says nothing**, for two reasons: he doesn't know what it means, and nobody asked. The log at the stone (protected). Camp on the road, no fire. The floor takes the last light like water, and Oryn holds her hands over the line until it's gone.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:28:- **Day 96, the perimeter (≈4,000, measured set piece):** procedure said once (Lira the instrument a stride inside; Karis on the line with the cord; Brom marking; Seln ahead; Oryn at the stone; Cael writing counts). The bend in Karis's wrist; **iron at the third cord**; sixty-two cords and twenty strides; ten cords to the middle; "A circle is a made shape." said once as geometry and not followed. **The stake**: registry stamp, thirty-one, a boot's width on the line, "Five years in the weather. A winter either side."; "You drive them where you've measured to."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:29:- **The trials at the stone:** Lira's full burst becomes a step ("It's in me. It's not in the air."; the clock line); Brom's "Skin."; Karis sees every point and can fill none ("It costs nothing. There's nothing to spend."); Seln vanishes for a breath without his Path ("It was never most of what I do."); **Oryn's three crossings** with Brom's arm in her hands ("Nothing in my hands" / "A healer's hands stop working there."). **Cael's two private tests:** the Iron read released before the stride, running across it; at twenty strides a foot's worth of Wind evasion round a stone. From behind it is a man stepping. "It was dark before. It's dark now." Both halves true; together not the truth.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:35:- The word *Quieting* does not exist yet. Say "the line", "quiet ground", "inside". "Made" is said once, by Karis.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:38:- No stillhound is seen; it is all sign. The movement ends at dusk at the far lip, about to move.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:43:The six-day road's incidents; the plank and the room; how the letters land; the void road's country; Thornwater's evening; the order and texture of the trials; the site's light; Teague's and Karis's windows.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:10:- POV: Cael ≈30,700. **Seln cutaway ≈1,800** (days 10–40: walking every road out of Lowmarch, and later out of Thornwater, alone, first, unasked; the report nobody asks for). **Teague cutaway ≈1,500** (day 49, the door: his three counted before the job, then the board, then the five; he finds Seln on the second pass). Teague's crew is never named, including in his head.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:24:- **C1 (default unless the owner rules otherwise):** in Lowmarch's first week the horse and cart are sold. A horse is fodder and a sign that says *paper*; the scrub ruts past Lowmarch take mules. The sale and what is left of the Book 6 purse become a sealed reserve that Brom's rule keeps them from living on. The log's "in hand" counts only what the board pays. Give it one good scene and an argument with a joke in it, then let it go.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:25:- **Lowmarch, day 9, and the board read like the Cinder House board.** Fourteen slips, not one pricing the crew. Pike: sixties, one arm, "Copper, Force, thirty years on the roads." "Walk, carry, climb, fight." / "In that order?" / "Depends on the day." A heading opened with five names and five columns: Job, Hirer, Witness, Outcome, Price. No tier column. He reads it upside down and looks for the missing column "the way you look for a stair in the dark, with a foot."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:28:- **The Thornwater road (days 41–43), ≈4,000:** the carter at the fire ("Two carts went quiet on it last month"); the stretch at dusk after a wheel cost an hour; positions; the valley's noise; **Lira's hand up at a hole in the noise**; Seln without turning, "Don't declare anything." / "Walk. Same pace."; "I could clear it." / "No." / "I know. I'm saying it so I've said it."; Brom becoming exactly as large as his body and no larger; Karis deciding five times not to take out the notebook; the five items (keeps station at forty meters; makes no sound; tracks the buckle; won't cross the gravel fan; reacts to nothing because they gave it nothing); it stops a hundred meters short of the fence. No blow struck.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:29:- **Thornwater:** the gate, the woman with the lantern, the bowman who doesn't point; "First crew I've hired that knew to shut up."; "Stillhound… You shut up. It went home."; "You're paper." / "Yes." / "Hm."; the slip marked; the grain loft; six days; the carter back on the fourth; Pike's copied line; the log with "Note the date. Season's open, and for once it isn't theirs."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:30:- **Lowmarch, day 49 — the board anatomized:** a woman captain's line read before and after; the eleven-bale captain ("Say it again and I'll write it"); "The book's for me. The saying's for them."; the wall at the lower inn; "A Bronze who lost my carter…"; "Did you ever hear of a ledger-keeper called Vell?" / "No."; Seln's finger on the carter's map, the asset-restriction **said once and put away**, the map turned east. "Four lines. Nobody lost, nobody hurt, nobody knows you." Brom: "Eleven."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:38:- The stillhound's sense is **unknown** in this movement. Karis has the word, not the mechanism; the discharge finding belongs to M2. Nobody hears the words *quiet ground*. No healer, no Tide practitioner, no Oryn.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:40:- Teague and Cael exchange no words. The Thornwater carter is never named.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:8:- Owner names: canon only. Teague's crew (including the older healer of no Path), the hide carter, the ferryman and his boy, the old woman at Thornwater, the carters at the fire and the inn's keeper stay unnamed. **The fourth site stays unnamed.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:9:- POV: Cael ≈29,900. **Teague cutaway ≈1,700** (days 117–120: following the crew's trail three days along a bearing he does not understand, the healer brought because a shoulder was mended once; sitting down beside the boy; the column). **Karis cutaway ≈2,000** (days 119–120 at the far fire: three copies, the ledger, the edge laid and moved; it ends exactly on the pencil stopping; no who or why). **Seln cutaway ≈1,600** (days 124–128, the road home: the ledger in his coat; giving it to Karis and not asking for it back). **Oryn cutaway ≈2,800** (day 122 to about 128: the gap north-west, four days, three weeks late; Thornwater; the old woman's knee; writing the letter, ending on its four lines).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:16:The Stair's rim on the 115th, with a bearing taken off two sites with a brass edge. Brom's shoulder is mended once, and Lira's arm is closed again. Six people and two mules. Teague's crew is turning back toward Millrace.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:23:- **The Drowned Hall from the rise:** roofless, twelve strides square, a spring through the broken floor, a marsh exactly as wide as the Quiet. "Third." **The line** at the marsh's edge ("Gone"/"Back"); **stake thirty-three** (old, and no second); mud **heaved from below** along the water's edge ("It's never been out."); a bar at the hall's lip **bent from below**, read from a hundred and seventy meters. **Oryn's lore**: "Big. Under. Comes up. Nobody's seen it whole."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:25:- **Day 119, the Hall (≈5,000–6,000):** Brom *stops* to put Karis up the wall and the floor opens under him; he puts her up before he goes sideways. "Get *off* the floor." **The coping** as cover and trap. Karis copying the wall she kneels on, funny for exactly one exchange. **Brom's shoulder opens**; he slips on the wrong wall. **Oryn into the water, skipping**, the healer reaching a falling patient (not heroic, only nearest). **The second pass turns** toward where she is going. **Cael in, declaring:** Compression takes the strike into a standing frame at the broken edge; **Anchor laid on the floor** at the broken centre. "A thing that hunts what stays commits to the thing that stays hardest." It surfaces whole for the first time in anyone's memory. "Brom. Wall. Your weight. Now." **Four bolts into the pale**: Lira twice, braced one-armed against the coping and a knee, with Seln spanning between (the bowman's lessons pay); Seln twice. The point released; the jaws close on water; it lets go and goes down, alive. "Walls… Twelve sheets." It is left there.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:26:- **Costs at the track's end:** Oryn's hour, "Twice…" (protected); the long sit, wet to the waist; his bill (Compression in the ribs, Anchor held against biting, the read at its dearest under water). **The exchange** (protected) ending "Lie still. I want to read you."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:27:- **Two days at the marsh (119–120):** two fires. Seln's blanket over Karis's shoulders. Lira keeps the bolt in the bow. Brom: "Twice." / "Twice." Oryn sleeps in front of people. **The second self-reading** (an hour; the banks a limit; **the still place**, named here for the first time; the river round a stone it has always known; four things he can count; protected log). The third before dawn: "the same." **Oryn changes the order**: "You in me." Asked and granted; surface, then a minute of the long one at her count, and while he is in, **he tells her exactly**; her finding (protected); "Write it down and stop touching it." **C3: Karis lays the cord at the Hall's perimeter** in the marsh between copies. **Teague's crew** along the track with a fifth: the older healer of no Path, "Twice?" / "Then it wants binding, not hands." The two women bind it. **Teague sits down beside him**, as Brom once did. "What are you." **The wrist a foot from his hand:** not the short reading, not the long one, not the asking. "Why did you stop reporting?" (protected exchange). "The board's going to need a new column." The log (protected). **The pencil stopping** at the far fire.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:29:- **The walk (121–122):** frost that rings; one cart of hides and a lifted hand; holds shut; the six catalogued because they will be five; the first night in a ruined hold's lee ("Twice." / "Twice." / "And not three."). **The fork:** "three weeks late there… I'm going back to being the route." He walks her fifty paces and does not ask. "Find me at Thornwater." / "Bring the map." **The four behind him, with one mule.** The log at the fork (protected).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:32:- **Lowmarch (129–131):** the fifth honest catalogue, from the landing. **The season line read** (protected); the ledger turned toward him; **no number**; "too small" (protected); the room's "Eleventh." / "Aye." **Teague's term** and "Noted." The healer's single look at Brom's shoulder. **The winter fence** given over ("Ours."). Karis takes the back room and pays without counting (ninety-six). **The inventory** (protected; the audio rule). **The last ferry**: nine pieces sorted aloud; **Hesk's straightedge** with the note (protected); the replies west (protected). **Oryn's letter by carter** the morning after (protected): "Six, by letter." "She'll say when." / "Spring." **The map**: four circles, the bearing, both edges laid along it, **touching the three paced centres for Cael exactly as for Karis**. "The sites were on an alignment. Not random." "Someone made this pattern." Four seconds. **The closing, exact.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:41:- Lira's order stands at first snow (Oryn "will say when"). The ankle is unmended. Brom's shoulder is bound, not mended a third time. Oryn's crossbow is with Lira, with one bolt left.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:51:Book 8 Ch1: Lowmarch with the ice coming and the ferry's ropes taken in. Ninety-six in hand. A kit on a table. A map with a line going off its edge. A healer at Thornwater with a route and an arm to release. A captain's spring term. A fourth circle twice the size behind a fence of iron. And a question asked once at a table that nobody answered.
