editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-APPLIED.md:225:- **Oryn's letter (Ch24):** *Route's whole. The knee held. Nobody died of three weeks. Spring: bring the map, and lie still when I say. — O.* — then: Six, by letter. (The architecture and series docs still quote "eleven days"; prose and Book 8 say **three weeks**. See C6.)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-APPLIED.md:231:- **Oryn's letter (Ch24):** *Route's whole. The knee held. Nobody died of three weeks. After the thaw: bring the map, and lie still when I say. — O.* — then: Six, by letter. (The architecture and series docs still quote "eleven days"; prose and Book 8 say **three weeks**. See C6.) [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-APPLIED.md:253:- Ch14, the birthday line: *Hundred and second day past the Line. Nineteen. Written at Thornwater, in the steading's common room, autumn, the fire lit for us. Witnesses: four of my own, and a healer who's a stop.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-APPLIED.md:259:- Ch14, the birthday line: *Hundred and second day past the Line. Nineteen. Written at Thornwater, in the steading's common room, the fire lit for us. Witnesses: four of my own, and a healer who's a stop.* [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-APPLIED.md:267:- Ch10: Karis: "Sixty-two cords and twenty strides," … "Twelve hundred and fifty-six meters, and a piece." … "A circle is a made shape." — Lira: "like a clock that stopped and started again without losing the time." — Seln: "You drive them where you've measured to. Not where you've measured from." … "Five years in the weather. A winter either side." — Brom: "Skin." — Karis: "It costs nothing. There's nothing to spend." — Seln: "I've a knife and fifteen years. It was never most of what I do." — Oryn: "Nothing. Not nothing in him. Nothing in my hands." … "A healer's hands stop working there." — Cael: "It was dark before," … "It's dark now." — Karis: "None I own. And I own more than the registry prints." — Seln: "They live in here because nothing that walks in can fight."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-APPLIED.md:273:- Ch10: Karis: "Sixty-two cords and twenty strides," … "One thousand three hundred and seventy-four yards, and a piece." … "A circle is a made shape." — Lira: "like a clock that stopped and started again without losing the time." — Seln: "You drive them where you've measured to. Not where you've measured from." … "Five years in the weather. A cold term either side." — Brom: "Skin." — Karis: "It costs nothing. There's nothing to spend." — Seln: "I've a knife and fifteen years. It was never most of what I do." — Oryn: "Nothing. Not nothing in him. Nothing in my hands." … "A healer's hands stop working there." — Cael: "It was dark before," … "It's dark now." — Karis: "None I own. And I own more than the registry prints." — Seln: "They live in here because nothing that walks in can fight." [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-APPLIED.md:281:- Ch20: Teague: "We'll hold it till you're up." / "Noted" — Oryn: "What are they" / Karis: "Lines," — Karis: "He tried to drive it. Twice, by the head. It wouldn't go. Nothing goes into this." — Seln: "Nobody leaves a registry kit. It's signed out. You don't get another." … "I don't know what this is in, and I'm not going to say." — Karis: "Forty-one," … "every ten cords and a piece. Two hundred meters and a stride, to the stride." … "The floor was carved by somebody who knew the circle's size," … "A measurement is a fact about a ruler, not about the hand that held it."
