editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:8:- Owner names: canon only. Thornwater's people stay unnamed.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:22:- **The Ring (≈8,000–9,500 across two chapters), a retreat with a geometry.** The line is the objective. Nine counted on the white. "The road's cut." / "The grass. Where the cord went." Brom holds the lip: a hand's-height drop that robs a hound of drive, the haft, a man the pack cannot hear. Lira runs the rim's turned edge; the ankle goes a third time; the forearm taken and held; she cannot burst it off. **Brom's bolt through the eye at four meters.** Oryn's hands: "Nothing… Nothing in my hands." Cloth and knees. "Move. I can't fix this here. Move." Brom's string opens his fingers in the dark. The lane counted down, 160 to 60, the scrub moving at Lira's pace and never showing a shape. They are *careless* in here, because no prey has ever shouted. **Karis down at sixty**, hands on a throat, the jaws closing across her fists, the loudest sound on the ring. **Shadow, once, ten strides** (circle and Oryn only). The throw. Then *he stops holding*: Wind full, north off the lane; every head turns; then everything, one after another, so there is never a breath when he is not the loudest thing on the floor. Pressure for noise; Ember held out; Blade ringing with nothing to cut; Storm seeding the rut; Anchor off its hold and looking west. North to the rut, **east the wrong way** about a hundred and twenty meters, back west. Seln's "Back" from the stone and Lira's a breath after. The second lock with Compression at contact. Over the stone. **The bolt at two meters.** Anchor's perception sees Karis's points before they light: **the wall of ignition along the line's inside edge**, from her knees, voiceless. Seven break out north and south along the outside; two dead. Win-sentence and costs on the page. The opponent learned nothing it could use, because it had never needed to.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:23:- **The hour's mending at the line by lantern:** "There. Back." (she does not mention the clock). The state, said because a thing not said is not a finding. **The order (protected, exact)** and the sling; "One arm. From here to the snow."; "The ankle's a tape and a season…"; Oryn flat on the road. Karis's written lines. Seln: "Nothing." Brom: "Hand." / "Morning. Wash it. I've nothing tonight." The log, including **the Book 9 plant line, exactly.** Close: "It worked in there." / "Yours." / "Yes." / "Later." / "Later."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:24:- **The camp at the stone (night of the 96th → dawn of the 98th):** the unfiled entry (protected). Morning arithmetic aloud: Karis's throat ("Days. Hoarse before it's anything."); Brom's hand ("String… That's two."); **Cael's calf read and not mended**, the fourth failure ("I don't say a finding four times to a patient and change it on the fifth."). Oryn against the stake: "Three in two days… That's a route." The route's far end, eleven days north. **Seln at the stake**: the charcoal circle from memory lies on the carter's circle; "Ignorance doesn't stamp iron."; "The Compact knows what quiet ground does. And it's filed somewhere we can't reach." (once); "No… I carried the maps. I never saw the file." Karis: *Where*, then *Entered as said*, then *Blank. Stamped. Filed.* **The contract re-read:** a question, not a recovery; "We just told them."; "Six is wrong. I'm a stop." / "They'll write six." The dead hound dragged off and the bolt cut out (five in the sleeve); rations in sixths; nobody says *yours*. Second-night log. **Dawn of the 98th: Oryn's eight crossings alone.** He watches and does not write it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:25:- **Two days back (98–99):** Lira walking flat-footed as she is told; the calf closing with no count on the flat by the second noon. **Thornwater:** "Six. Well." Tape off in the yard ("Twenty-one days. A rib is six weeks. These are done."). The calf closed in four days. "Still and whole." / "You don't get a yes. You get told." / "What does helping look like?" / "I'll know."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:32:- Nobody theorizes why the fragments work inside. "Later" holds until M6. *Quieting* still does not exist.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:30:- **Where/when:** Lowmarch in first snow on the 129th day past the Line. The ferry's last run on the 130th. Oryn's letter by carter on the morning of the 131st. Book 8 Ch1 opens on the 131st.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:31:- **Cael:** **nineteen** (turned on the page on the 102nd, at Thornwater). **Ten confirmed fragments.** The tenth is **Tide-adjacent** (Oryn; partial; Iron; self and contact; *Engagement: clinical — non-hostile*), acquired on the 100th. The anomaly is now **a location, not an entry: the still place.** It was read three times. It does not flow and does not change, and everything goes around it. It is not the Quiet and not a fragment. Not touched since a healer said *stop*. Ribs quiet again since the marsh. Calf a closed seam.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:33:- **Lira:** left forearm bitten through at the Ring, mended at the line, reopened on the Stair and closed again. **Still slung and under Oryn's order at first snow** ("She'll say when"). Right ankle taped and **never mended in this book.** Carries Oryn's crossbow on its strap (hers from the Hall, Ch21).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:35:- **Karis:** holds the field archive: **52 sheets** of copied walls (Ring 11 / Stair 29 / Hall 12); the kit's **field ledger** (given her by Seln on the road home); the carter's map with **four circles and the bearing**; the Ternhall straightedge. She named the Quieting. Her hypothesis stays unentered. She has the inn's back room for the sheets.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:37:- **Oryn:** at Thornwater on her route, **three weeks late there** and the route whole. Letter: "Six, by letter." She learned the mechanism on the 100th. She has not heard any theory, because there is none.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:40:- **Teague:** "Spring. Whatever's on that bearing. My crew comes." / "Noted." His crew (four plus an older healer of no Path) winters at Lowmarch. He has given the axe-head hold's long fence (forty, HOLD) to the five for the winter.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:43:- **The Quieting, as known:** four sites on one alignment. The Fallow Ring, the Long Stair and the Drowned Hall have been entered. The fourth was paced from outside on the 123rd: **four hundred metres' radius**, ringed by a **cordon of iron stakes numbered thirty-four, with the stroke-and-bar mark, a pace apart**. Not entered, not named, its effect unknown, its central shape a standing grey thing nobody has a word for. "Someone made this pattern." was said once and not answered.
